<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Generated from crates/escouade-policy/src/list.rs (cargo run -p escouade-policy --example generate): do not edit. -->
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Escouade</displayName>
  <description>Escouade’s policies for managed devices.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="escouade">Escouade</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_ESCOUADE_2_3">Escouade 2.3 and later</string>
      <string id="cat_permissions">Permission modes</string>
      <string id="cat_harnesses">Harnesses and models</string>
      <string id="cat_plugins">Plugins</string>
      <string id="cat_editor">Editor</string>
      <string id="cat_features">Features</string>
      <string id="cat_projects">Projects</string>
      <string id="cat_network">Proxy and certificates</string>
      <string id="cat_privacy">Telemetry and voice</string>
      <string id="cat_remote">Remote Control</string>
      <string id="cat_updates">Updates</string>
      <string id="cat_servers">Servers</string>
      <string id="cat_mcp">Outside MCP clients</string>
      <string id="cat_enrollment">Enrollment</string>
      <string id="permissions_allowBypass">Deny the Bypass mode</string>
      <string id="permissions_allowBypass_Explain">The mode where a harness asks nothing (bypassPermissions) is no longer allowed to any agent. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › Agents › “Allow Bypass mode”, off and grayed; the Bypass mode refused everywhere.

Key: permissions.allowBypass (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="permissions_modes">Allowed permission modes</string>
      <string id="permissions_modes_Explain">The list of the modes agents may take: plan, default, acceptEdits, auto, bypassPermissions. An agent in another mode ends its turn, then goes to the nearest allowed mode.

On the device: The modes not allowed grayed in “Default mode of agents”, the board’s mode and an agent’s mode.

Key: permissions.modes (list, among plan, default, acceptEdits, auto, bypassPermissions). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="permissions_defaultMode">Default agent mode</string>
      <string id="permissions_defaultMode_Explain">The mode of new agents: plan, default, acceptEdits or auto. It stays within the allowed modes: outside them, the nearest allowed one.

On the device: Settings › Agents › “Default mode of agents”, grayed.

Key: permissions.defaultMode (string, plan, default, acceptEdits, auto). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="permissions_defaultMode_plan">plan</string>
      <string id="permissions_defaultMode_default">default</string>
      <string id="permissions_defaultMode_acceptEdits">acceptEdits</string>
      <string id="permissions_defaultMode_auto">auto</string>
      <string id="harnesses_allowed">Allowed harnesses</string>
      <string id="harnesses_allowed_Explain">The list of the harnesses agents may use, by their id (claude, codex, copilot, cursor, opencode, gemini…). An agent of a harness no longer allowed stops at the end of its turn.

On the device: The harness of a project, an agent, a ticket: a harness not allowed is grayed and refused.

Key: harnesses.allowed (list). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="harnesses_allowedModels">Allowed models by harness</string>
      <string id="harnesses_allowedModels_Explain">A JSON object that gives, for each harness, the list of its allowed models. A harness absent from the object keeps all its models.

On the device: An agent or a ticket on a model not allowed is refused at its start.

Key: harnesses.allowedModels (JSON). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort">Maximum effort</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort_Explain">The highest effort an agent may be given: low, medium, high, xhigh or max.

On the device: The effort of the board’s agents brought down to this ceiling; a higher effort refused.

Key: harnesses.maxEffort (string, low, medium, high, xhigh, max). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort_low">low</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort_medium">medium</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort_high">high</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort_xhigh">xhigh</string>
      <string id="harnesses_maxEffort_max">max</string>
      <string id="plugins_allowedOrigins">Allowed plugin origins</string>
      <string id="plugins_allowedOrigins_Explain">Where a plugin may be installed from: store-verified (the store, verified versions), store (the store, any version), team-store (the team’s store), git, folder (a folder), dev (a folder in development).

On the device: Installing a plugin of another origin is refused and said.

Key: plugins.allowedOrigins (list, among store-verified, store, team-store, git, folder, dev). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="plugins_allowed">Allowed plugins</string>
      <string id="plugins_allowed_Explain">The list of the plugin ids that may be installed. Absent, all may.

On the device: Installing a plugin outside the list is refused and said.

Key: plugins.allowed (list). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="plugins_denied">Denied plugins</string>
      <string id="plugins_denied_Explain">The list of the plugin ids that are never installed, even when allowed elsewhere.

On the device: Installing a plugin of the list is refused and said.

Key: plugins.denied (list). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="plugins_verifiedOnly">Install verified versions only</string>
      <string id="plugins_verifiedOnly_Explain">A version of the store without the “Verified by Escouade” seal is refused, at an install as at an update. Only the value true (1) is imposed.

On the device: Plugins › “Install verified versions only”, on and grayed.

Key: plugins.verifiedOnly (Boolean, true (1)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="plugins_projectSettings">Imposed plugin settings in each project</string>
      <string id="plugins_projectSettings_Explain">A JSON object: its keys are plugin ids, its values the settings of project scope this device imposes in each project where the plugin is on (dev.acme.ci, level: strict). A simple setting only (text, number, boolean, choice): never a secret, a profile, a value imported nor a setting its author keeps off the files; such a setting is ignored and said. A team imposes its own by its file (plugins.id.key).

On the device: Projects › Plugins, the setting grayed with the padlock and Imposed by this device’s policy; the plugin reads the imposed value.

Key: plugins.projectSettings (JSON). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="secrets_fileFallback">Deny the file of the plugins’ secrets</string>
      <string id="secrets_fileFallback_Explain">On a device without a system keychain, a plugin’s secret can no longer be kept in a file readable by its user alone: only the keychain keeps it. A file already chosen is no longer read; its secrets move to the keychain or are erased with it. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: “Keep in a file only you can read” is no longer offered at a secret’s field, and Plugins › “Secrets kept in a file” bears the padlock.

Key: secrets.fileFallback (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="extensions_allowed">Editor’s allowed extensions</string>
      <string id="extensions_allowed_Explain">A JSON object like VS Code’s extensions.allowed: its keys are * (all), a publisher of Open VSX or an extension (publisher.name), its values true, false, stable (no pre-release) or the list of the versions allowed. The most precise key says it. An object that names anything allows only what it names. It adds to the lists of the settings and of the .escouade.yml files: an extension must be allowed by each.

On the device: General › “Editor’s allowed extensions”, grayed; an extension outside the list is refused before any download, and an installed extension it leaves out is no longer loaded.

Key: extensions.allowed (JSON). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="projects_forcePrivate">Private projects by default</string>
      <string id="projects_forcePrivate_Explain">Every project is private: its agents see no other project, and no other project sees it. Only the value true (1) is imposed.

On the device: “New projects are private” and each project’s “Private project”, on and grayed.

Key: projects.forcePrivate (Boolean, true (1)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="accounts_reservation">Account reservation</string>
      <string id="accounts_reservation_Explain">denied: no account is reserved to a project; a private project goes on the shared accounts, its fence keeps its sessions. required: a private project goes only on an account reserved to it alone, never on a shared account, even at the limit.

On the device: denied: each account’s “Reserved to projects” emptied and grayed, “Reserve … to this project” and “Add a reserved account…” refused. required: “Shared accounts at the limit” off and grayed, “Stop reserving it” refused on the last account reserved to a private project, an agent of a private project refused on a shared account.

Key: accounts.reservation (string, denied, required). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="accounts_reservation_denied">denied</string>
      <string id="accounts_reservation_required">required</string>
      <string id="projects_maxParallel">Ceiling of the tickets in parallel</string>
      <string id="projects_maxParallel_Explain">The most tickets “In progress” at once in each project’s Kanban, from 1 to 64. It lowers the machine’s bound (16 on a desktop, 64 on a server), never raises it; between this device and the team, the lower one holds.

On the device: Settings › Kanban › “In parallel” goes no higher, the ceiling and where it comes from said under the setting; set_board refuses higher, and a Kanban set higher starts no more tickets than the ceiling.

Key: projects.maxParallel (number, 1–64). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="projects_deniedFiles">Denied file patterns</string>
      <string id="projects_deniedFiles_Explain">File patterns (the .gitignore way) agents neither read nor write, added to those of the projects.

On the device: Read and kept; applied to the agents with a project’s fence of files (to come).

Key: projects.deniedFiles (list). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="proxy_url">Proxy address</string>
      <string id="proxy_url_Explain">The HTTP(S) proxy of the app, the plugins and the agents, for example http://proxy.example.com:3128.

On the device: Settings › Advanced › Network, the proxy’s address grayed.

Key: proxy.url (string). Sort: sensitive.</string>
      <string id="proxy_exclusions">Proxy exclusions</string>
      <string id="proxy_exclusions_Explain">The hosts reached without the proxy (NO_PROXY), one per line.

On the device: Settings › Advanced › Network, the exclusions grayed.

Key: proxy.exclusions (list). Sort: sensitive.</string>
      <string id="proxy_denyInsecureTls">Deny skipping the TLS check</string>
      <string id="proxy_denyInsecureTls_Explain">“Skip TLS certificate verification” is off and can no longer be turned on. Only the value true (1) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › Advanced › Network › “Skip TLS certificate verification”, off and grayed.

Key: proxy.denyInsecureTls (Boolean, true (1)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="proxy_authorities">Certificate authorities file</string>
      <string id="proxy_authorities_Explain">The path of a .pem file of authorities trusted besides the system’s store (a corporate proxy’s root).

On the device: Settings › Advanced › Network › “Extra certificate authorities”, grayed.

Key: proxy.authorities (string). Sort: sensitive.</string>
      <string id="telemetry_enabled">Turn the usage statistics off</string>
      <string id="telemetry_enabled_Explain">The anonymous statistics are no longer sent. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › General › “Usage statistics”, off and grayed.

Key: telemetry.enabled (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="voice_onlineAllowed">Deny online voices</string>
      <string id="voice_onlineAllowed_Explain">The dictation and the conversation’s voice stay on the device (Whisper and Piper): no online service. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › Voice, “Online” brought back to local (Whisper, Piper) and refused.

Key: voice.onlineAllowed (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="voice_dictation">Turn the dictation off</string>
      <string id="voice_dictation_Explain">The dictation no longer starts. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › Voice › Dictation, grayed; the dictation refused.

Key: voice.dictation (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="remoteControl_enabled">Deny the Remote Control</string>
      <string id="remoteControl_enabled_Explain">No agent is reachable from claude.ai. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: “Remote control for all agents”, a project’s and an agent’s, off and grayed.

Key: remoteControl.enabled (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="updates_channel">Stable channel only</string>
      <string id="updates_channel_Explain">No beta version is offered. Only the value stable is imposed.

On the device: Settings › General › “Receive beta versions”, off and grayed.

Key: updates.channel (string, stable, beta). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="updates_channel_stable">stable</string>
      <string id="updates_channel_beta">beta</string>
      <string id="updates_automatic">Turn automatic updates off</string>
      <string id="updates_automatic_Explain">A new version is offered, never installed by itself: the IT department deploys its own. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › General › “Install updates automatically”, off and grayed.

Key: updates.automatic (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="servers_allowed">Allowed servers</string>
      <string id="servers_allowed_Explain">The addresses of the team servers and the servers in server mode the app may reach. Absent, all.

On the device: A server outside the list is refused, with the reason.

Key: servers.allowed (list). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="servers_personalSpace">Deny the personal space</string>
      <string id="servers_personalSpace_Explain">Only the servers of the allowed servers’ list are added as spaces; without the list, none. This device stays a space. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: A server outside the list is refused before any connection, with the reason.

Key: servers.personalSpace (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="servers_aggregateView">Deny the aggregate view</string>
      <string id="servers_aggregateView_Explain">The “Everywhere” view shows only the numbers of a work server (of the allowed servers’ list, or any server without one), no text nor gesture. Set on a server, it holds for it. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: “Everywhere” gives only the numbers of these spaces.

Key: servers.aggregateView (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="servers_contentlessNotifications">Notifications without content</string>
      <string id="servers_contentlessNotifications_Explain">The notifications from a work server (of the allowed servers’ list, or any server without one) say an agent is waiting, never what. Set on a server, it holds for it. Only the value true (1) is imposed.

On the device: The notifications of these spaces carry no text.

Key: servers.contentlessNotifications (Boolean, true (1)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="servers_remoteApi">Deny the remote API</string>
      <string id="servers_remoteApi_Explain">The core’s remote API (the server mode, the phone) does not turn on on this device: no other device drives it. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: The remote API refused at its start and at each connection.

Key: servers.remoteApi (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="servers_phone">Deny the access from the phone</string>
      <string id="servers_phone_Explain">The phone’s WireGuard tunnel (ESC-567) does not turn on on this device nor on a server that receives it: no UDP port opened, nothing in the box, no API on the Tailscale address. The server mode through SSH stays allowed. Only the value false (0) is imposed.

On the device: Settings › Phone, off and grayed; a tunnel that is on turns off at once.

Key: servers.phone (Boolean, false (0)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="mcp_externalClients">Outside MCP clients</string>
      <string id="mcp_externalClients_Explain">What Claude outside Escouade (an outside MCP client) may do through Escouade’s MCP server: denied (nothing), readOnly (read only), allowed (everything). Escouade’s own agents are not concerned.

On the device: An outside client refused at its connection (denied), or its tools that write refused (readOnly).

Key: mcp.externalClients (string, denied, readOnly, allowed). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="mcp_externalClients_denied">denied</string>
      <string id="mcp_externalClients_readOnly">readOnly</string>
      <string id="mcp_externalClients_allowed">allowed</string>
      <string id="team_server">Team server</string>
      <string id="team_server_Explain">The address of the company’s team server: the member only has to accept their invitation.

On the device: Kept by the app; the screen to join the team will fill it in (to come).

Key: team.server (string). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="team_fingerprint">Team fingerprint</string>
      <string id="team_fingerprint_Explain">The fingerprint of the team expected on the team server: a team of another fingerprint is refused.

On the device: Kept by the app; checked when joining the team (to come).

Key: team.fingerprint (string). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="team_onlyThisServer">Refuse any other team server</string>
      <string id="team_onlyThisServer_Explain">Only the team server the policy sets may be joined. Only the value true (1) is imposed.

On the device: Another team server is refused, with the reason.

Key: team.onlyThisServer (Boolean, true (1)). Sort: restrict. “Disabled” removes the policy: the setting is free again.</string>
      <string id="team_maxOfflineHours">No new team agent without contact for N hours</string>
      <string id="team_maxOfflineHours_Explain">An agent of a team’s project no longer starts when its team’s server has not answered for this many hours: a circuit breaker set meanwhile cannot be missed. Personal projects are not touched.

On the device: The start of a team agent is refused, with the hour of the last contact; the team’s band says it.

Key: team.maxOfflineHours (number, 1–720). Sort: restrict.</string>
      <string id="features_kanban">Kanban feature</string>
      <string id="features_kanban_Explain">Tickets, the autopilot and ticket sources: true turns it on, false turns it off (its tab, its MCP tools, its autopilot). Its tickets are kept.

On the device: Settings › Features › Kanban, grayed.

Key: features.kanban (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_editor">Editor feature</string>
      <string id="features_editor_Explain">Opening, editing and searching the project’s files: true turns it on, false turns it off (the editor view, Ctrl P, its language servers).

On the device: Settings › Features › Editor, grayed.

Key: features.editor (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_docs">Docs space feature</string>
      <string id="features_docs_Explain">The specification, decisions, documents and discussions: true turns it on, false turns it off (its tab, its MCP tools). Its pages are kept.

On the device: Settings › Features › Docs space, grayed.

Key: features.docs (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_cost">Cost feature</string>
      <string id="features_cost_Explain">The cost of turns, agents and tickets, and the cache temperature: true turns it on, false turns it off.

On the device: Settings › Features › Cost, grayed.

Key: features.cost (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_stats">Statistics feature</string>
      <string id="features_stats_Explain">Activity and spending over time: true turns it on, false turns it off (its view). It has nothing to do with telemetry (telemetry.enabled).

On the device: Settings › Features › Statistics, grayed.

Key: features.stats (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_workflows">Workflows feature</string>
      <string id="features_workflows_Explain">A project’s chains of agents and skills: true turns it on, false turns it off (its tab, its MCP tool, their reading).

On the device: Settings › Features › Workflows, grayed.

Key: features.workflows (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_scheduled">Scheduled tasks feature</string>
      <string id="features_scheduled_Explain">Tickets that come back at a set time: true turns it on, false turns it off (its tasks no longer run). It also goes with the Kanban.

On the device: Settings › Features › Scheduled tasks, grayed.

Key: features.scheduled (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_overseer">Overseer feature</string>
      <string id="features_overseer_Explain">The agent that drives every project: true turns it on, false turns it off (its screen, its shortcut, its MCP tools; it stops).

On the device: Settings › Features › Overseer, grayed.

Key: features.overseer (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
      <string id="features_voice">Voice feature</string>
      <string id="features_voice_Explain">Dictation and spoken conversation: true turns it on, false turns it off (the microphone, its shortcut, the listening).

On the device: Settings › Features › Voice, grayed.

Key: features.voice (Boolean, true, false). Sort: value.</string>
    </stringTable>
